WEBVTT

00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:13,820
Do you mention herbs or meopathy for nausea?

00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:17,820
If I prescribe nausea meds with my chemo,

00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:21,820
should I get these other options to try first?

00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:27,820
I think it's always good to try non-medications

00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:31,820
before trying medications.

00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:36,820
You have to be honest

00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:41,820
and say that lots of times medications are going to work better,

00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,820
but they're not without side effects.

00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:49,820
I don't think anybody can argue that pain meds

00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:52,820
can do a great job of taking care of pain,

00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,820
can get rid of my pain.

00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,820
Probably better than anything else,

00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:01,820
especially if I got serious pain,

00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,820
but it also comes with side effects.

00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:08,820
You always try to do things as natural as possible

00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:11,820
for all sorts of reasons.

00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:14,820
So I would definitely try that first,

00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:17,820
but I would go ahead and take the prescription,

00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,820
so you have it,

00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:22,820
and if you have to use it, you have to use it,

00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:25,820
but using some of the herbs and meopathy

00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:29,820
for some symptoms can be helpful.

00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:32,820
The ones for nausea can be helpful.

00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:36,820
But I mean people that are other anti-dose medication

00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:39,820
over the years, and they're still in horrible nausea,

00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,820
and they use both.

00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:45,820
So everybody's a little bit different that way.

